<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Portuguese Mombasa</h1><p class="st-meta">1593 CE – 1698 CE · capital Mombasa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Portugal's main stronghold on the Swahili coast, centred on Fort Jesus, which fell to Oman after a siege of nearly three years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After decades of hostility with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a>, the Portuguese occupied the island in 1593, built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> to an Italian design and installed the ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malindi">Malindi</a> as sultan. The fort became the headquarters of Portuguese power north of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mozambique">Mozambique</a>, guarding the routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A Portuguese captain commanded the fort and collected customs, while a client <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> sultan governed the town. Relations were tense: in 1631 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-al-hasan">Yusuf ibn al-Hasan</a>, raised as a Catholic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> as Dom Jeronimo Chingulia, returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, massacred the Portuguese garrison and briefly held the fort before abandoning it. Catholic missions had little lasting success.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/omani-empire">Omani Empire</a>, after expelling the Portuguese from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a>, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> from 1696 until it fell in December 1698. Portugal briefly regained it in 1728 to 1729, but <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> passed to Omani governors and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mazrui-sultanate">Mazrui Sultanate</a>. Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1593 CE – 1698 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.40%;width:2.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1593 CE – 1698 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mombasa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yusuf ibn al-Hasan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese, Swahili</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kenya">Kenya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Portuguese East Africa (Mombasa), Captaincy of Mombasa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1646&amp;focus=portuguese-mombasa" aria-label="Portuguese Mombasa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5781 2329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Portuguese Mombasa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6101 2585L6101 2585M6101 2585L6114 2554M6101 2585L4773 1044M6101 2585L6562 1563"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6101 2585h0M6114 2554h0M4773 1044h0M6562 1563h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6101 2585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6101 2585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mombasa. <a href="/atlas?year=1646&amp;focus=portuguese-mombasa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
